  "Question": "In which direction does \\(y^2=4x\\) open?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "To the right",
    "B": "To the left",
    "C": "Upward",
    "D": "Downward"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(y^2\\) equals a positive number times \\(x\\), so the focus lies on the positive x-axis and the parabola opens to the right.\n\nAlternative method 1: Use nonnegative squares\n\nRewrite the equation as \\(x=y^2/4\\). Thus \\(x\\ge0\\), with equality only when \\(y=0\\), and opposite values of \\(y\\) give the same \\(x\\). The vertex is the origin, and as \\(|y|\\) increases, both branches extend farther in the positive \\(x\\)-direction. Therefore the parabola opens to the right, choice A.",
